saQut Compiler — Language-Independent Compiler Toolbox

USAGE:
  saqut <command> [file] [options]
  saqut -                          (stdin mode — TODO)

COMMANDS:
  run        run program (token → AST → IR → VM)
  tokens     print token list
  ast        print AST hierarchy and analysis as JSON
  symbols    print symbol table (functions, variables)
  check      semantic analysis — type checking + structural validation
  ir         print IR instruction list (intermediate representation)
  exec       evaluate an expression and print the result  (saqut exec "1+2")
  lsp        start LSP server (JSON-RPC on stdin/stdout)
  dap        start DAP debug adapter (JSON-RPC on stdin/stdout)
  bench      phase-level benchmark (tokenize|parse|symbol|typecheck|ir|vm)
  compile    TODO: compile source to binary
  parse      TODO: generate IR
  transpile  TODO: transpile to C code

OPTIONS:
  -o, --output <file>    Output file
  --format <json|text>   Output format (default: text)
  -h, --help             Show this help

EXAMPLES:
  saqut run source.sqt
  saqut tokens source.sqt
  saqut ast source.sqt --format=json
  saqut symbols source.sqt
